        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: دلخور",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دلخور (delkhor) — \"upset (with someone)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خواهرم از حرف من دلخور است. khâharam az harf-e man delkhor ast. My sister is upset at what I said."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The cause takes az: az kasi delkhor budan. Built on del 'heart' and khor, the stem of khordan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "delkhor is built on two native Persian pieces, usually explained as del, 'heart', and khor, the present stem of khordan, 'to eat': a heart that is eaten at. EtymDB traces del to Middle Persian (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
